    <div class="msg-payload">
      
          <pre class="wordwrap">Hi Chenguang,

The procedure in Section 6 seems reasonable to me. I tried it against
BEST (draft-dinuzzo-best-protocol-02), a protocol with a well-known
JSON manifest, which runs on several production services, including
one built independently of me. BEST only speaks to your &quot;known domain&quot;
context.

There are gaps in my protocol, but they are easy to fix. The TXT
record is not implemented in our tools yet, and freshness information
will be added. Regarding Entity Type, the protocol uses the
CloudEvents specification, so the information is there.

Regards,
Riccardo

Il giorno dom 1 nov 2026 alle ore 08:54 Du Chenguang
&lt;du_chenguang@outlook.com&gt; ha scritto:
&gt;
&gt; Hi all,
&gt;
&gt; The charter asks DAWN to specify the minimum public discovery
&gt; information, and how we decide what belongs in it seems worth
&gt; discussing early. In draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model-01 we made a first
&gt; attempt: for each of the charter&#x27;s three deployment contexts, we
&gt; asked what a client needs to use a discovery result (choose one,
&gt; fetch its description, talk to it, or ask a catalog for more), and
&gt; treated only that as the minimum.
&gt;
&gt; <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/" rel="nofollow">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/</a>
&gt;
&gt; We would welcome your views on whether this is a reasonable way to
&gt; determine the minimum, what other approaches we should consider, and
&gt; whether the resulting elements match your mechanisms and use cases.
&gt;
&gt; Best,
&gt; Chenguang
&gt; _______________________________________________
&gt; Dawn mailing list -- <a href="mailto:dawn@ietf.org">dawn@ietf.org</a>
&gt; To unsubscribe send an email to <a href="mailto:dawn-leave@ietf.org">dawn-leave@ietf.org</a>
</pre>

      
    </div>
    <div>
      
    </div>
</div> <!-- msg-body -->




